notes:QUEUED EXECUTION DIRECTIVE 2026-07-28: Compare Kotlin/JVM versus Kotlin/Native as required by the task, but honor the product requirement that the compiled CLI driver target is Kotlin/Native unless evidence proves the accepted native-executable-v1 boundary cannot be met, in which case retire the identifiers explicitly rather than silently switching to JVM. Build from accepted TASK-260728-2spy93, TASK-260728-1g0z69 and TASK-260729-rhjxtx evidence. Select paired local/external identifiers, trusted Kotlin/Native root/konanc identity, version/target normalization, compatibility families, artifact and distribution layout, cache/receipt/marker identity, and fail-before-compiler ordering. There is no legal ecosystem manifest measured for pure metadata and Gradle scripts execute code: specify a neutral manager-owned metadata surface consistent with skill-build.json/local build_roots or fail closed; no generic Gradle/Maven/KSP/plugin/script/annotation/cinterop/network escape hatch, package-selected toolchain/path/env/channel/install/trust input, or auto-install. Define deterministic macOS/Windows/Linux qualification rules while keeping current Kotlin/Native host evidence UNVERIFIED and making no false platform claim. Preserve frozen releases; no stage/commit/publish/pin; hand off with exhaustive allow/reject matrix and deterministic evidence.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-338c0b, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-338c0b)\nDeveloper run started. Host inventory confirms rhjxtx: no Kotlin/Native distribution on this macOS host (kotlinc-native, konanc, ~/.konan all absent); Kotlin 2.4.10 JVM-backend CLI and OpenJDK 26.0.1 are present. Measured evidence collected under .temp/TASK-260728-168smo/evidence: (1) the shipped Kotlin CLI launcher is a bash wrapper that resolves bash, uname, dirname and java from PATH (4 resolutions under a shim PATH); invoking the fingerprinted JDK java directly with -cp into the Kotlin distribution records 0 PATH resolutions and produces the artifact, exit 0. (2) A bare @-prefixed argument expands as a response file: a build-root file named @inject containing -script plus a .kts source caused the compiler to EXECUTE package code, exit 0. Absolute and ./-prefixed forms of the same path do not expand (exit 1, source entry is not a Kotlin file). (3) JDK_JAVA_OPTIONS and JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS are honoured by the JVM launcher; both notices go to stderr and java --version stdout line 1 stays stable. Task-owned curator-spec worktree created at .temp/TASK-260728-168smo/curator-spec-worktree from clean 57c1f56.\nDeveloper handoff ready for review.\n\nDECISION: Kotlin/Native selected as the v1 artifact model; every Kotlin/JVM shape deferred. Thin JAR, fat JAR (-include-runtime) and jlink/jpackage images all fail decision 0008 section 3 as runtime-bundle: a fat JAR is one file and still not directly loadable by the host program loader, so one file is necessary and not sufficient. GraalVM native-image rejected on four independent grounds (second compile-phase command, third toolchain outside decision 0007 closed set, classpath needs a package manager or a package-controlled member, different backend requiring a different family segment). Identifiers adopted unchanged from decision 0008 section 2: kotlin-native-v1 and kotlin-native-repository-v1. jdk is a REQUIRED companion under a NATIVE model, correcting decision 0007 expectation table, because the Kotlin/Native compiler is JVM-hosted while the produced artifact needs no runtime.\n\nMEASURED (macOS 26.5 / kotlinc-jvm 2.4.10 / OpenJDK 26.0.1; no Kotlin/Native distribution on any reachable host):\n1. @argfile expansion is an ACE channel. A build-root file named @inject containing -script plus a .kts caused the compiler to execute package code, exit 0. Absolute and ./ forms do not expand (exit 1). A missing argfile is a warning with exit 0, so partial mitigation fails silently. Rejection matrix is therefore a closed ALLOW-LIST over name shapes (directories, *.kt, one kotlin-native-module.json, leading-character class excluding dotfiles and @), with absolute-path argv as a measured structural backstop, not as the rule.\n2. Shipped launcher is inadmissible: 4 PATH resolutions (uname, dirname, java -version, java <compile>) plus shebang bash, and it reads six environment channels including KOTLIN_COMPILER which selects the compiler main class. Direct <jdk_root>/bin/java -cp <kotlin_root>/... records 0 PATH resolutions, exit 0, artifact produced. Driver never runs any launcher script, including for the version probe.\n3. Kotlin has no lawful project-metadata file, so the driver mints kotlin-native-module.json {schema_version, kotlin_version}, closed, never passed to the compiler. Stage B classifier is two classes rather than Rust seven; security partition F empty so P1/P2 collapse to C = Upstream.\n4. jdk probe pinned to java --version on stdout: single stream and byte-stable under JDK_JAVA_OPTIONS/JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS injection, both of which were measured to be honoured.\n\nPLATFORM POSITION: platforms and compatibility are EMPTY for both identifiers and both registry entries. No tuple claimed, macOS included. Eight named obligations (K-1..K-8) and a Q1-Q9 acceptance test that requires the control run to fire. macOS is not admitted if any Xcode/usr-bin executable is spawned; Windows forbids cmd/powershell/link.exe/cl.exe/lib.exe/vswhere/VS activation; Linux waits on TASK-260728-1skseh then TASK-260728-3u1nho. Retirement trigger fixed: if no tuple passes Q1-Q9 when TASK-260728-251p01 mints manifest schema 8, both identifiers retire unused and claim schema 4 is minted over six.\n\nREVIEWER ITEMS: (a) decision number 0010 taken because 0009 is claimed concurrently by TASK-260728-12pnm1 and TASK-260728-1jafds; renumbers rather than contests. (b) The narrow reading of decision 0007 section 3 under the JVM-hosted launcher shape (kotlin root contributes no launcher process; primary executable is the companion bin/java) is recorded explicitly as a completion within the section 1.3 mandate, not a widening; if decision 0007 owner rejects it, the consequence is retirement, not a compensating wrapper.\n\nGATES (real exit codes, each standalone): spec validate.py baseline 57c1f56 = 0; spec validate.py task worktree = 1 (expected-red, 3 broken links all in two copied-in in-flight docs, 0 from this task; scoped check over the two authored documents = 0, 4 links); spec unittest = 0; spec go test ./tools/... = 0; curator go build = 0; go vet = 0; go test = 0; gofmt ./cmd ./internal = 0; make check = 2 (expected-red, gofmt stage on four vendored files under .temp/TASK-260720-1zntv0, this task authored 0 Go files). golangci-lint NOT RUN: not installed on this host.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-338c0b, pid=24078, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 DIRECTIVE: Independently review the Kotlin/Native artifact-model and driver-pair decision; do not edit producer artifacts. Challenge whether this is truly a host-loadable Kotlin/Native executable model and whether an empty platform matrix plus retirement trigger is an honest, implementable contract rather than a speculative identifier reservation. Verify the manager-owned kotlin-native-module.json surface, direct trusted JDK java invocation, Kotlin root/JDK companion identity, exact process graph, closed source and argv shapes, response-file mitigation, environment scrubbing, artifact extraction, cache/receipt/marker identity, and local/external equivalence. Attempt escape channels through Gradle/Maven/scripts/plugins/KSP/annotation processors/cinterop/network/package-selected paths, flags, toolchains, response files, launchers and host utilities. Reproduce the measured controls where the host permits; distinguish unverified platform obligations from accepted semantics. Reconcile decision 0007 compatibility and decision numbering, and publish a decisive verdict with exact changes if rejected.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-49361f, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-49361f)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 VERDICT — CHANGES REQUESTED. Kotlin/Native remains the only valid artifact class and the JVM deferral plus closed Gradle/Maven/KSP/plugin/script surfaces are sound, but the pair is not implementable. A checksum-verified official Kotlin/Native 2.4.10 macOS arm64 distribution proves the compiler is JVM-hosted with no regular kotlin-primary executable, while accepted decision 0007 requires the primary executable inside the primary entry root. Its konan.properties names remote LLVM/sysroot/toolchain/LLDB inputs. Direct offline compilation with empty KONAN_DATA_DIR exited 2 on missing lldb-4-macos, produced no artifact, and mutated the directory with dependencies/.extracted and cache/.lock, contradicting Q4 and the [kotlin,jdk] process/cache identity. Registry probe/baseline/relpath/companion/compatibility/platform fields remain unresolved, and distribution platform klibs make the stdlib-only/no-C-interop statement incomplete. Rework in analysis: measure one exact trusted closure, resolve the primary-executable invariant, specify/fingerprint a complete offline dependency bundle and interop policy, then pass at least one Q1-Q9 tuple or retire both identifiers now. Evidence: TASK-260728-168smo_review-verdict-cycle-1.md\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-49361f, pid=54764, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 DIRECTIVE (review cycle 1): Preserve the accepted Kotlin/Native choice, JVM rejection, closed package surfaces, @argfile defence and local/external equivalence, but replace the non-implementable official-archive-as-toolchain model. Use the checksum-verified 2.4.10 evidence and attempt a closed operator-curated Kotlin/Native bundle compatible with decision 0007: one fingerprinted primary kotlin root may contain the JDK runtime, Kotlin compiler archive, fully prehydrated LLVM/sysroot/target/additional-tools/LLDB dependency closure and a fixed regular primary executable relpath; do not treat downloaded mutable state or an external companion executable as implicitly trusted. Specify immutable bundle layout/provenance/fingerprints, exact process and executable closure, operation-private writable overlay, no-download proof, dependency locks/cache identity, exact version/target probes and normalization, compile argv/output, compatibility family, receipt/cache binding and install guidance. Independently measure an official distribution plus dependencies on macOS arm64, pass Q1-Q9 for at least that tuple or provide evidence that the pair must retire under the accepted invariant; mark Windows/Linux unsupported or unverified with exact reasons, never placeholders. Close distribution-owned platform .klib/native-interop imports and dynamic-link consequences through an explicit allow/reject policy. Fill every registry field, update decision/reference/results/probe evidence and preserve frozen releases. No stage/commit/publish/pin; hand off for fresh review only with a real offline compile, zero network, bounded mutation proof and exact child-process evidence.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-571491, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260728-571491)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 COMPLETE — ready for review.\n\nOUTCOME. The Kotlin/Native artifact model is now MEASURED, not argued: a real macos_arm64 compile produced app.kexe (785,672 B, Mach-O arm64), it runs, and every dynamic dependency is a base-installation library. That is the affirmative answer decision 0008 section 10 asks this task to establish. All Kotlin/JVM shapes stay rejected.\n\nTRUSTED ROOT REPLACED. The non-implementable official-archive-as-toolchain model is gone. The kotlin root is now an operator-curated bundle curator-kotlin-bundle-v1: jdk/ + kotlin-native/ + prehydrated konan-data/, immutable and fingerprinted whole, primary_relpath jdk/bin/java. Decision 0007 section 3 is satisfied literally, so the cycle-1 narrow reading is WITHDRAWN. The jdk companion is dropped entirely: one root, one digest, one-element toolchain_identities; the jdk identifier stays reserved and unmapped.\n\nMEASURED AND FILLED. Probe konanc -version writes Kotlin/Native: 2.4.10 (22 B) to stdout, exit 0 — the anchored rule now asserts the BACKEND token, which a JVM distribution cannot satisfy. baseline at_least 2.4.10. Default target from konanc -list-targets (default) line. -o app produces app.kexe plus an app.kexe.dSYM by-product. Hydrated closure byte-unchanged by a compile (1470 files, same aggregate SHA-256); read-only data dir fails on dependencies/cache/.lock; symlink overlay over a read-only bundle works; airplaneMode=true fails closed with no download; full network denial with a hydrated closure exits 0 with zero download lines. Dependency hydration is an operator act outside every operation.\n\nMACOS IS EXCLUDED, AND IT IS PROVEN. Exec containment to the bundle roots fails at CurrentXcode.bash(Xcode.kt:144). The complete external set for a hello-world is /bin/bash, /usr/bin/xcode-select, /usr/libexec/PlistBuddy, /usr/bin/xcrun, Xcode xcodebuild, Xcode ld, Xcode dsymutil, plus the Xcode SDK as sysroot; with all seven allowed it exits 0. With ignoreXcodeVersionCheck=true and every Apple property overridden to absolute local paths it still spawns /usr/bin/xcrun at AppleConfigurablesImpl.getAbsoluteTargetToolchain(Apple.kt:45). Cause is structural: konan.properties declares the Apple toolchain/sysroot/addon as remote:internal and XcodePartsProvider has only InternalServer (KONAN_USE_INTERNAL_SERVER, repo.labs.intellij.net) and Local (the host Xcode). Second independent ground: the Xcode SDK is an unfingerprinted build input, so two hosts with different Xcode versions alias in the cache key. macos/arm64 and macos/amd64 are therefore permanently unsupported at Protocol 1.0, not pending.\n\nPAIR NOT RETIRED, AND WHY. The reviewer asked for one qualified tuple or retirement now. Neither is available honestly. The measurement proves an APPLE-TARGET failure and shows in the same properties file that targetToolchain/targetSysRoot for mingw_x64 and linux_x64 resolve under KONAN_DATA_DIR/dependencies with no remote:internal and no host SDK. Retiring on macOS evidence would assert a negative about two tuples never measured — the same class of error as claiming them — and retirement is one-way for the whole protocol version because decision 0008 section 2 closes the identifier space. The hard trigger is retained and sharpened: if no tuple passes A1-A9 when TASK-260728-251p01 mints manifest schema 8, both identifiers retire unused.\n\nTWO REVIEW FINDINGS PRODUCED CONTRACT CHANGES, NOT WORDING. (a) The @-response-file defence was stated wrongly: expansion is decided by the argv tokens FIRST CHARACTER, and @/abs/path/file DOES expand. Absolute paths are safe because they start with /, and the driver must never emit an @-prefixed token. (b) The stdlib-only/no-C-interop claim was false: import platform.posix.* and platform.Foundation.* link with no -library and no .def and add a dynamic dependency. The surface is now explicitly ALLOWED (it is inside the fingerprint and cannot be package-extended) and its consequence is bound by a NEW published-artifact dynamic dependency gate — the manager reads the produced files dynamic dependency list in staging before hashing and fails build_artifact_class_unsupported outside the tuple allow-list. Reading headers is not executing.\n\nBOARD. Created TASK-260729-2vfvgi run-windows-kotlin-driver-pair-qualification under this story, with a written justified-gap record and spec/out-of-scope self-verification, blocked by this task plus the two Curator implementation tasks. windows/amd64 is now the only tuple that can admit the pair. A link making TASK-260728-251p01 blocked by it was rejected by the board as a cycle; the obligation is carried normatively in decision 0010 section 14 instead. Sequencing consequence for the story owner: TASK-260728-r3j8ef and TASK-260728-1aveb2 cannot run a Kotlin build on macOS and must move to the qualified host.\n\nGATES (real exit codes). spec validate.py baseline 57c1f56 = 0 (30 schemas, 93 vectors); spec validate.py task worktree = 1 EXPECTED-RED, 3 broken links all in two copied-in in-flight sibling docs, 0 from this task; link sweep scoped to the two documents authored here = 0 (6 links); spec unittest = 0 (8 tests); spec go test ./tools/... = 0; curator go build = 0; go vet = 0; gofmt ./cmd ./internal = 0 files; curator go test ./... = 0. golangci-lint NOT RUN (not installed). This task authored two Markdown documents and no Go, schema, vector or release file. No staging, commit, publication or pin.\n\nHOST. The 889 MB distribution and its 688 MB hydrated dependency closure were downloaded into .temp/TASK-260728-168smo/kn and DELETED after measurement; the archive was deleted after checksum verification. No toolchain installed, no PATH or profile touched, ~/.konan never created, free disk restored.\nagent completed: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-571491, pid=72567, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 2 DIRECTIVE: Independently review the operator-curated Kotlin/Native bundle rework and replay its evidence without editing producer artifacts. Verify curator-kotlin-bundle-v1 is a reproducible, immutable, whole-tree fingerprinted root containing JDK, Kotlin/Native and fully prehydrated konan-data; primary_relpath jdk/bin/java must satisfy decision 0007 literally, with no untrusted launcher, external companion, mutable hydration state, package-selected env or download. Recompute exact version/default-target probes, bundle mutation/network-denial evidence, operation-private writable overlay behavior, argv/response-file rules, artifact extraction/by-products, cache/receipt/marker identity and local/external source equivalence. Challenge the permanent macOS exclusion by replaying the Xcode/xcrun process and unfingerprinted-SDK findings, and verify that allowing bundled platform klib imports plus the produced-artifact dynamic-dependency gate is complete and fail closed. Adjudicate the empty current platform matrix and deferred retirement trigger: confirm it neither falsely qualifies Windows/Linux nor leaves non-implementable reserved identifiers; audit the new windows/amd64 qualification task, dependencies, A1-A9 gate and schema-8 retirement boundary. Check every registry field and decision numbering, replay applicable gates, publish exact ACCEPTED or CHANGES REQUESTED evidence and route accordingly. No product edits, staging, commit, publish, pin, toolchain install or platform-claim widening.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-4fc5ea, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-4fc5ea)\nREVIEW CYCLE 2 VERDICT — CHANGES REQUESTED. Route to analysis. Kotlin/Native selection, JVM deferral, curated single-root closure, and macOS exclusion are retained. Blocking gaps: accepted decision 0007 requires this task to supply a qualified-host registry entry but platforms/compatibility remain empty; konanc -list-targets is required by compile/cache identity but absent from the declared Stage A probe; the directory allow-list admits gradle/KSP/kapt/META-INF paths that section 7.2 and A8 claim are rejected; and the probe archive final allow-list has six paths while prose claims an exact seven-process inventory. Qualify one tuple and fill every field, or retire both identifiers now; correct the target probe, rejection matrix, and process evidence. Evidence: TASK-260728-168smo_review-verdict-cycle-2.md\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260729-4fc5ea, pid=17898, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 3 DIRECTIVE (review cycle 2): Preserve the accepted Kotlin/Native artifact choice, JVM deferral, curator-kotlin-bundle-v1 single-root trust model, local/external equivalence, and permanent macOS exclusion. Close every blocking finding now. Use the available root-capable Windows host via `ssh win` to attempt an exact windows/amd64 A1-A9 qualification in a private temporary directory using checksum-verified upstream inputs; do not install system-wide, alter persistent PATH/profile, or leave mutable toolchain state. If and only if that tuple passes, populate every registry platform/compatibility/relpath/probe/artifact/overlay field and bind the measured tuple into cache, receipt, marker and acceptance vectors. If qualification cannot be completed or any guarantee fails, retire both Kotlin identifiers now rather than retaining an empty reservation. Independently add package-neutral Stage A default-target discovery with exact argv/stream/bounds/grammar/exactly-one rule/token mapping/typed failures and bind it to host-pair validation, compile argv and identities; make the Gradle/KSP/kapt/META-INF/services classifier and rejection matrix deterministic and consistent; replace the inconsistent macOS six-versus-seven claim with a complete resolved-path process trace or make only evidence-supported non-completeness claims. Update all task-scoped decision/reference/results/evidence, run applicable gates, and hand off for fresh review. Do not edit frozen release files, stage, commit, publish, pin, install host software, or widen Rust/Swift/Kotlin implementations.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260729-4d0a9a, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (claude) (run=RUN-260729-4d0a9a)\nCYCLE 3 PROGRESS: Windows host (ssh win, Windows 10 Pro 19045.6456, AMD64, admin) is reachable and is being used for the windows/amd64 A1-A9 attempt in a private temp dir C:\kn168. Checksum-verified inputs: kotlin-native-prebuilt-windows-x86_64-2.4.10.zip 222,016,219 B sha256 ce99eba1f4faec1d77f4bbd747bb722404ef11f2c349ec70c59d4c002859380f MATCHES published .sha256 asset; Temurin OpenJDK21U-jdk_x64_windows_hotspot_21.0.11_10.zip 205,073,954 B sha256 d3625e7cadf23787ea540229544b6e2ab494b3b54da1801879e583e1dfee0a64 MATCHES Adoptium API checksum. Measured so far: Windows distribution contains ZERO .exe files (13 bin entries, all .bat or shell scripts) so the vendor archive fails decision 0007 section 3 on Windows too; curated bundle jdk/bin/java.exe is a regular 50,344 B executable; konanc -version stdout is 23 B Kotlin/Native: 2.4.10 with CRLF (22 B LF on macOS) exit 0; konanc -list-targets stdout 131 B, 8 lines, exactly one (default) marker on mingw_x64, stderr empty, exit 0; konan.properties mingw_x64 toolchain/sysroot resolve to $toolchainDependency.mingw_x64 = msys2-mingw-w64-x86_64-2 with no remote:internal; hydration downloaded exactly 4 dependencies (lldb-2-windows, msys2-mingw-w64-x86_64-2, llvm-21-x86_64-windows-essentials-150, libffi-3.3-windows-x64-1) and -o hyd produced hyd.exe 570,368 B, exit 0. Review finding 4 root cause identified from the cycle-2 archive: run8 final allowed-externals.txt legitimately holds SIX paths (the sufficient set for the successful path); xcodebuild appears only in run7 where xcode-select was denied, so the external set is path-dependent and the exactly-seven prose claim is wrong and will be corrected to a measured union plus a sufficiency statement.
